    description: "The LARGEST remaining chunk of INV-nuzas's phantom-workspace-external residual (52 of the 107; distinct from WI-hotug's call-reached CASE A/B). Self-analysis: 52 external_symbol nodes with a workspace prefix are reached by module_attr_ref edges (a non-call attribute READ on an imported module constant), minted by _emit_module_attr_refs (py.py ~3273-3314) — but wait: _emit_module_attr_refs only fires for `module_imports` (import X) receivers, so these 52 come from a DIFFERENT path. INVESTIGATE the exact emission site (grep the module_attr_ref emitters); likely an attribute read `CONST.attr` (not a call) where CONST is `from x import CONST` and attr is accessed without calling, OR a multi-segment `mod.CONST.field` chain.\n\nFIX (mirror WI-hotug CASE B): when the module_attr_ref receiver resolves via the import-anchored _lookup_symbol_by_module to an in-tree kind=variable symbol (allow_ambiguous=False, INV-fahub, + a `not in _caller_locals` scope-shadow guard), retarget the module_attr_ref edge to the in-tree variable node instead of minting a workspace-prefixed phantom external. Coherence: check the module_attr_ref->variable partition (module_attr_ref IS in TAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES, so unlike WI-hotug's references edge, retargeting a module_attr_ref to an in-tree variable may interact with taint — verify the taint findings are unchanged, and whether references vs module_attr_ref is the right retarget type). Acceptance: drives the INV-nuzas phantom count 68 -> ~16 (52 closed). Re-measure INV-nuzas after landing."  # f626
