  message: "LANDED — PR merged, dev 6d50b100b0. _emit_module_attr_refs now retargets a non-call attribute read on an imported IN-TREE module constant to a references/ast_name_read edge to the real kind=variable, instead of the phantom workspace external. Three INV-fahub-critical choices: (1) EXACT module match (global_symbols.get), not suffix _lookup_symbol_by_module — a suffix match would bind an external 'import json as j; j.X' to a coincidentally same-suffixed in-tree pkg/json.py (mirrors WI-hotug CASE A); (2) edge type 'references' NOT 'module_attr_ref' — module_attr_ref IS in TAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES, so retargeting it to a live in-tree node would inject a new taint frontier; the adversarial review ran a before/after verify-claims diff and confirmed Python taint findings byte-IDENTICAL (the 52 phantoms matched 0 attributes:-catalog stdlib IO primitives); (3) shadow guard.\n\nTWO adversarial-review fixes were load-bearing: (a) the shadow guard EXCLUDES plain 'import X as Y' aliases (_collect_local_bindings(include_import_aliases=False)) — a function-local 'import pkg.mod as m; m.CONST' (the DOMINANT self-corpus shape: a test method importing then reading) is the alias to resolve, not a shadow; without this the retarget closed only 3 of 52. (b) The walk is now SCOPE-BOUNDED (skips nested def/class bodies) — a raw ast.walk descends into nested scopes and under the retarget mints a confidently-wrong RESOLVED edge attributed to the enclosing function / over a nested param shadow.\n\nBehavioral (self-analysis): module_attr_ref-reached workspace phantoms 52 -> 18; total INV-nuzas workspace phantoms 58 -> 24. Coherence-neutral (un-allow-listed offenders 28, unchanged). 100% cov; smart-test 3795 passed. Residual 18 = kind=function/dunder/re-export targets the variable-only guard correctly skips. Follow-up WI-luhah: the enclosing-scope closure-capture + module-scope-rebind shadow gaps (contrived; shared with the sibling _emit_variable_refs)."  # 7a51
